{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.93fd2924031e7f6efbde0a09.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Responsibility for soundness and record keeping is read substantively alongside the express obligation to ensure proper records and compatibility.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.93fd2924031e7f6efbde0a09.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"An outcome-sensitive reading does not by itself establish strict liability for every incident.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":null,"candidate_id":"candidate.27299f062cf84d09aaeb000375bdcdf3","controlled_language":"Paragraph 10 can instead be read as requiring the Product Provider to secure the substantive soundness and ownership-record outcomes for which it remains fully responsible. A conclusion of fulfillment would require evidence connecting retained authority and exercised supervision to satisfactory operations and records under an applicable standard. No such standard or actual facts are supplied, so neither fulfillment nor a universal no-failure guarantee can be concluded.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["definitions"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.66389bca91c94e92a92f404b1a01a20e","issue.2d49726da4a543d4a92ebe53bbc3ca3d"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"In the same case of active supervision but defective ownership records, retained authority would not justify declaring paragraph 10 fulfilled: the substantive subject of responsibility remains deficient. Conversely, accurate vendor records alone do not show that the provider retained responsibility. The rival readings differ over what paragraph 10 itself demands, not whether separate record-keeping duties matter.","run_id":"run.8adc12b432874c5bb1e8b4730a0ab93f","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"d74180e126dda06342060a17b37c3227fc695e9fc0f0d5ce68b187d7cb8bc612","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u0.0","dc689bdf0ffcf.u1.224","dc689bdf0ffcf.u2.729","dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Paragraph 10 as substantive responsibility for performance"}